I will write a python script `work/extract_features.py` to process the video frame-by-frame (sampling at 5 frames per second). For each frame, it will warp the chessboard to an 800x800 image, calculate the mean RGB values of the center 40x40 region of each of the 64 squares, and save these time-series features to a file. This will give us a complete history of the visual state of each square.
I will run the feature extraction script. This will run in the background and write the JSON file.
